# {{SLUG}} — Design System (scaffold baseline)

This product was scaffolded by MC with a real component library, so UI work
starts from accessible, tokenized primitives — **not vibe-coded raw elements.**
This file is the **acceptance contract** for the scaffold and the handoff point
to the S0.2 artifact contracts.

## Stack

- **Next.js** (App Router) · **React 19** · **TypeScript** (strict)
- **Tailwind v4** (`@import "tailwindcss"` + `@tailwindcss/postcss`)
- **shadcn/ui** components (copy-in source under `src/components/ui/`)
- **Radix UI** primitives (accessibility) · **Lucide** icons

## What ships

| Layer | Where | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Design tokens | `src/app/globals.css` | CSS custom properties + `@theme inline`; light + `.dark`. **Single source of color/radius truth — never hardcode a hex.** |
| Class merge | `src/lib/utils.ts` (`cn`) | Tailwind-aware conflict resolution; all components compose through it. |
| Primitives | `src/components/ui/` | `button`, `card`, `input`, `label`, `dialog` (baseline). |
| Hardening | `next.config.ts` | Security headers (X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, HSTS). |

## Extend (do NOT hand-roll)

Add more primitives with the standard tool — they land in `src/components/ui/`
and inherit the tokens automatically:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add select dropdown-menu popover tabs toast
```

Never inline a raw `<button>`, `<input>`, or `<select>`; compose an existing
primitive (or add one) so tokens, focus rings, and a11y stay consistent.

## Contract linkage — S0.2 artifact contracts (`schemas/contracts/`)

This scaffold is the concrete surface the product-studio chain lands on:

- **`design_brief`** (`owner: design_quality`) — its `visual_hierarchy` is realized
  by the tokens in `globals.css` + the primitives here; its `mobile_requirements`
  are realized by the responsive utilities (Tailwind breakpoints) + the `mobile`
  Playwright project. The Wave-2 **design-quality gauntlet** approves the built UI
  against `design_brief`.
- **`build_spec`** (`owner: engineering`) — its `components[]` MUST reference
  primitives that exist in `src/components/ui/` (this baseline set, plus anything
  added via `shadcn add`). A `build_spec` naming a component with no `ui/` source
  is a contract defect (a builder hand-rolled it).
- **`acceptance_criteria`** (in `build_spec`) verify against this library + tokens.

> A component library is **not** the design owner (the gauntlet is) — but it is the
> substrate the gauntlet judges against. This file documents that substrate.
